OS uses namespaces to divide resources amongst processes
    good for process isolation from a security perspective

systemd is a process on the linux machine that controls
    other processes. It divides the kernal from the user
    it's one of the first processes to start upon boot

CRON process:

crontabs is a process started during boot
crontabs require 6 specific values:
    MIN -what minutes to execute at
    HOUR -what hour to execute at
    DOM -what day of the month to execute at
    MON -what month of the year to execute at
    DOW -what day of the week to execute at
    CMD -The actual command that will be executed
Use the * wildcard to intentionally omit a value
crontab generator and cron guru are sites that will
    generate your syntax for you if needed
use crontab -e to edit the user's crontab file
